	<monogr>
		<title level="m">Find $\\cos A$.&quot;, &quot;action&quot;: [&quot;Let $AD=a$ and $BC=b$. So, we know that $a+b+360=640$. So, $a+b=280$</title>
		<imprint/>
	</monogr>
	<note>The perimeter of $ABCD$ is 640 $\\triangle ABD$, we have $BD^2=a^2+180^2-2(a)(180)\\cos A$ $\\triangle BCD$, we have $BD^2=b^2+180^2-2(b)(180)\\cos A$ So, $a^2+180^2-2(a)(180)\\cos A=b^2+180^2-2(b)(180)\\cos A$ Now, we can cancel out $180^2$ from both sides So, $a^2-2(a)(180)\\cos A=b^2-2(b)(180)\\cos A$ Let&apos;s subtract $a^2$ from both sides.&quot;], &quot;action&quot;: &quot;So, we get $-2(a)(180)\\cos A=-2(b)(180)\\cos A-a^2+b^2$.&quot;, &quot;label&quot;: 1.0}</note>
</biblStruct>

